# Files whose exact BYTES are load-bearing.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true on the Windows machines this repository is developed
# on, which means git may rewrite line endings between the working tree and the
# blob. For most files that is invisible and welcome. For these four it is not:
#
#   - docs/api/openapi.v1.json is the frozen contract, and docs/api/index.html
#     records a sha256 of it.
#   - docs/api/index.html embeds a copy of that contract and records hashes of
#     the two vendored Swagger UI files beside it.
#   - apps/api/scripts/check-openapi-page.mjs fails the build when any of those
#     hashes disagrees with the file it names.
#
# A line-ending rewrite changes the bytes, therefore the hash, therefore the
# verdict — and it would do so on one platform and not the other, producing a
# gate that is green on the machine that ran the generator and red in CI, for a
# difference in no content anybody changed. `-text` tells git to store and check
# out these paths verbatim everywhere.
docs/api/openapi.v1.json     -text
docs/api/index.html          -text
docs/api/swagger-ui-bundle.js -text
docs/api/swagger-ui.css      -text
